  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Three fourths of a pitcher is filled with pineapple juice. The pitcher is emptied by pouring an equal amount of juice into each of \\(5\\) cups. What percent of the total capacity of the pitcher did each cup receive?",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(5\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(10\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(15\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(20\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(25\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "c",
    "value": "15"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-8-2020-p5.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Each cup receives one fifth of the \\(\\dfrac{3}{4}\\) of a pitcher, or \\[ \\dfrac{1}{5}\\cdot\\dfrac{3}{4}=\\dfrac{3}{20}=15\\%. \\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Each cup gets one fifth of \\(\\frac{3}{4}\\) of the pitcher",
        "Convert \\(\\frac{3}{20}\\) to a percent"
      ],
